# Cursor: the terminal is Shell, sub-agents are Task, questions are AskQuestion,
# and plan mode is entered by switching modes rather than by a dedicated tool.
# Task names no model per dispatch, so Claude's `model:` tier clause is dropped (conventions §11.6).
AskUserQuestion	AskQuestion
`Agent`	`Task`
\bBash\b	Shell
CLAUDE\.md	AGENTS.md
CLAUDE	AGENTS
, `model:` the (?:READ|EXEC|PLAN) tier value, omitted when empty	
multiSelect	allow_multiple
subagent_type: Explore	subagent_type: explore
# The two fan-outs that name general-purpose write files, the panel's reviews and
# the readers' notes, and Cursor publishes no file-writing built-in type: explore
# only reads. They dispatch with no subagent_type, as STAR's writing delegates do.
 \(`subagent_type: general-purpose`\)	 with no `subagent_type` set (Cursor publishes no built-in type that writes files)
